    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST01-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST01-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: ALM-ST01-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Applies to ST01_FILLING. Fictional equipment details and synthetic training instructions; not manufacturer instructions. Existing iMAKS limits are retained. No intrusive repair or isolation sequence is supplied." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST01-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST01-001 §FILL-PRS-LO warning" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/RULE-ST01-03>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST01_FILLING_PRS>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "FILL-PRS-LO warning. ST01_FILLING: A valid running ST01_FILLING_PRS reading below 3.3 bar and at least 3.0 bar activates fictional FILL-PRS-LO. RULE-ST01-03 requires inlet-valve inspection within five minutes. For a lone operator, the permitted first inspection is the external position indicator in EQ-ST01-001. If that time window has elapsed, record the overdue check; do not report it as completed." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST01-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST01-001 §FILL-PRS-LL critical" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST01_FILLING_PRS>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "FILL-PRS-LL critical. ST01_FILLING: A valid running ST01_FILLING_PRS reading below 3.0 bar activates fictional FILL-PRS-LL. SOP-002 specifies inspect and notify maintenance. The simulated controller additionally requests a quality-hold stop; that is a fictional scenario policy, not an iMAKS emergency-stop rule. Confirm actual machine state through telemetry. Acknowledgement does not clear the alarm or authorize product release." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST01-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST01-001 §Flow context and trend" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/maintenance/MAINT-04>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/MAINT-04>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/RULE-ST01-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST01_FILLING_FLW>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Flow context and trend. ST01_FILLING: RULE-ST01-01 requires ST01_FILLING_FLW between 112 and 128 L/min; SOP-002 has a low critical boundary of 105 L/min. Flow below 112 but at least 105 L/min activates fictional FILL-FLW-LO in this replay. MAINT-04 requires pressure below 3.3 bar for more than fifteen minutes before inspecting filter and pump. Sparse low samples twenty minutes apart do not prove continuous low pressure; confirm duration from a complete trend or report it unknown. Pressure and flow falling together cannot establish the root cause." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST01-001-s5> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST01-001 §Freshness and lifecycle" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Freshness and lifecycle. ST01_FILLING: At the selected replay time, use only observations at or before that time. Good-quality telemetry is fresh for thirty seconds inclusive. Each alarm instance remains active until an explicit cleared lifecycle event appears. Stopped zero flow is expected and cannot establish normal delivery. Falling stopped pressure does not establish depressurization, and old nominal readings cannot authorize restart." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST02-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST02-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: ALM-ST02-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Applies to ST02_SEALING. Fictional equipment details and synthetic training instructions; not manufacturer instructions. Existing iMAKS limits are retained. No intrusive repair or isolation sequence is supplied." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST02-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST02-001 §SEAL-TMP-HI warning" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/RULE-ST02-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST02_SEALING_TMP>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "SEAL-TMP-HI warning. ST02_SEALING: ST02_SEALING_TMP values greater than 195 degrees C and at most 210 degrees C activate fictional code SEAL-TMP-HI while the controller is running. RULE-ST02-01 requires temperature within 175 to 195 degrees C. A warning is not permission to operate outside that band. Apply TRB-ST02-001; do not wait for the critical trip when the operating band is exceeded." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST02-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST02-001 §SEAL-TMP-HH critical trip" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/RULE-ST02-02>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST02_SEALING_TMP>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST03_LABELLING>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "SEAL-TMP-HH critical trip. ST02_SEALING: A valid ST02_SEALING_TMP reading greater than 210 degrees C activates fictional code SEAL-TMP-HH. RULE-ST02-02 and SOP-002 require emergency stop of ST02_SEALING, ST03_LABELLING, and ST04_PACKAGING and inspection. An alarm record documents the controller request, not proof that all affected stations stopped. The supplied replay never exceeds 210 degrees C and contains no critical-trip event." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST02-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST02-001 §Instrument limit advisory" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/TMP-2210>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Instrument limit advisory. ST02_SEALING: Fictional code SEAL-TMP-RANGE activates above the installed TMP-2210 continuous maximum of 200 degrees C and requests engineering review. It is a scenario-specific advisory, not an existing iMAKS critical rule. SPEC-ST02-001 explains the gap between the 210 degrees C critical threshold and the 200 degrees C continuous instrument rating. A numeric display outside the continuous rating is evidence of the controller report, not a verified accurate process temperature." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST02-001-s5> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST02-001 §Freshness and alarm lifecycle" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Freshness and alarm lifecycle. ST02_SEALING: Use only records at or before the explicitly selected replay time. Fresh telemetry has good quality and age from 0 through 30 seconds. Good quality is the controller transport flag; it does not certify accuracy beyond the instrument rating. Alarms remain active until an explicit cleared lifecycle event exists. Cooling after stop and acknowledgement do not clear them. Missing or stale measurements block a recovery claim." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST04-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST04-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_VIB>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: ALM-ST04-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Synthetic demo alarm-code mapping for ST04_PACKAGING and ST04_PACKAGING_VIB. Limits reproduce the existing graph's SOP-001 and SOP-002 values; alarm codes are fictional additions." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST04-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST04-001 §Warning: PKG-VIB-HI" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/RULE-ST04-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_VIB> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Warning: PKG-VIB-HI. For ST04_PACKAGING_VIB, PKG-VIB-HI activates when a valid running vibration measurement is greater than 0.20 mm/s and at most 0.35 mm/s. RULE-ST04-01 requires maintenance within 24 hours. An active critical alarm takes precedence over this warning response. A warning alone does not establish a bearing defect or authorize maintenance work by an operator. Follow TRB-ST04-001 to establish the current state." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST04-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST04-001 §Critical: PKG-VIB-HH" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/RULE-ST04-02>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_VIB> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Critical: PKG-VIB-HH. For ST04_PACKAGING_VIB, PKG-VIB-HH activates when a valid running vibration measurement is greater than 0.35 mm/s. RULE-ST04-02 specifies emergency stop and bearing inspection. In this simulated controller, the event requests a protective stop and latches the critical alarm. Confirm the actual stopped state on HMI-ST04; an alarm event alone does not prove that the machine stopped. If motion continues or an immediate hazard is visible, use the local emergency stop and keep clear. Acknowledgement does not permit restart." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST04-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST04-001 §Trend advisory and uncertainty" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/maintenance/MAINT-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/MAINT-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_VIB>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Trend advisory and uncertainty. MAINT-01 on ST04_PACKAGING is the SOP-003 maintenance action to inspect and lubricate the main bearing when ST04_PACKAGING_VIB drifts upward by more than 0.05 mm/s over 60 minutes. Compare valid running readings at matching speed. The advisory identifies a maintenance need, not a confirmed root cause. Stopped readings must not be used to establish bearing recovery. Vibration can also reflect a loose sensor or a mechanical obstruction; this dataset does not confirm either." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST04-001-s5> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST04-001 §Freshness and alarm lifecycle" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Freshness and alarm lifecycle. For the ST04_PACKAGING demo replay, evaluate records only at the explicitly selected scenario time. A telemetry sample is fresh if its age is between 0 and 30 seconds inclusive and quality is good. Do not use future records. A pre-stop peak can explain the trip but is not a current running measurement. An alarm remains active until an explicit cleared lifecycle record exists; a zero stopped vibration reading does not clear it. Missing, stale, or bad-quality evidence blocks a recovery claim. Consult REC-ST04-001 for restart conditions." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/DS-MECH-4400-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "DS-MECH-4400 §1. Pressure Transmitter PRS-4410" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/PRS-4410> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "1. Pressure Transmitter PRS-4410 Parameter Value Unit Measuring range 0 to 10 bar Accuracy (total error) ±0.10 bar (±0.075% FS) Repeatability ±0.025 bar Long-term stability ±0.05/year bar Media temperature -10 to +80 °C Application Note — Alarm Threshold Setting: With a total accuracy of ±0.10 bar, alarm thresholds should be set at least 5× the accuracy (0.50 bar) from the nominal operating point to avoid nuisance alarms. Thresholds closer than 3× accuracy (0.30 bar) are not recommended for process control." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/DS-MECH-4400-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "DS-MECH-4400 §2. Electromagnetic Flowmeter FLW-4450" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/FLW-4450> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "2. Electromagnetic Flowmeter FLW-4450 Parameter Value Unit Measuring range 0 to 500 L/min Accuracy ±0.5% of reading — Max fluid temp +80 °C" .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/DS-MECH-4400-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "DS-MECH-4400 §3. Piezoelectric Accelerometer VIB-4480" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/VIB-4480> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "3. Piezoelectric Accelerometer VIB-4480 Parameter Value Unit Measuring range 0 to 50 mm/s RMS Frequency range 10 to 1000 Hz Accuracy ±3% of reading Resonant frequency ≥ 18 kHz" .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/DS-MECH-4400-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "DS-MECH-4400 §4. Inductive Speed Encoder SPD-4490" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/SPD-4490> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "4. Inductive Speed Encoder SPD-4490 Parameter Value Unit Speed range 0.1 to 10 m/s Resolution 0.001 m/s Max amb. temp 80 °C" .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/DS-THERM-2200-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "DS-THERM-2200 §1. Temperature Sensor TMP-2210 — Specifications" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/TMP-2210> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "1. Temperature Sensor TMP-2210 — Specifications Parameter Value Unit Notes Measurement range -40 to +200 °C Continuous; see note 1 Accuracy (IEC 60584) ±1.5 (class 2) °C At 20°C reference Response time (t90) < 3 s In still air Output signal 4–20 mA Linear to range Max intermittent 220 °C < 10 min; not for control Note 1 — Maximum Operating Temperature: The rated maximum for continuous operation is 200°C. Exposure above this value accelerates thermocouple ageing and may cause drift of up to ±5°C within 500 hours. For applications requiring sustained operation above 200°C, ThermoSense recommends the Series 2400 (Pt100 RTD, rated to 250°C continuous)." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/DS-THERM-2200-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "DS-THERM-2200 §2. Humidity Sensor HUM-2250 — Specifications" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/HUM-2250> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "2. Humidity Sensor HUM-2250 — Specifications Parameter Value Unit Measurement range 0 to 100 %RH Accuracy ±2.0 %RH Operating temp -20 to +60 °C Response time < 8 s" .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/EQ-ST01-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "EQ-ST01-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: EQ-ST01-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Applies to ST01_FILLING. Fictional equipment details and synthetic training instructions; not manufacturer instructions. Existing iMAKS limits are retained. No intrusive repair or isolation sequence is supplied." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/EQ-ST01-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "EQ-ST01-001 §Equipment and process path" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST01_FILLING_FLW>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST01_FILLING_PRS>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/FLW-4450>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/PRS-4410>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Equipment and process path. ST01_FILLING: For PO-1001, the fictional product path is inlet valve VLV-ST01-01, filter FLT-ST01-01, pump PMP-ST01-01, and filling manifold MAN-ST01-01. ST01_FILLING_PRS, model PRS-4410, measures delivery pressure downstream of the pump. ST01_FILLING_FLW, model FLW-4450, measures delivered flow. The instrumentation measures process delivery pressure, not a pneumatic supply. No upstream-pressure sensor or filter differential-pressure measurement is supplied." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/EQ-ST01-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "EQ-ST01-001 §Operator observation points" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Operator observation points. ST01_FILLING: HMI-ST01 outside the closed guard provides Diagnostics, Alarm History, Stop, and Alarm Acknowledge. OBS-ST01-01 is the external inspection window facing the inlet valve position indicator and pump status lamp. The valve OPEN/CLOSED/UNKNOWN indicator can be read without access. If obscured, record not visible. Do not infer valve position from pressure. The emergency-stop control is beside HMI-ST01." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/EQ-ST01-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "EQ-ST01-001 §Lone-worker scope and tools" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Lone-worker scope and tools. ST01_FILLING: The trained operator may read the HMI, command normal Stop, record evidence, and observe the external indicators without tools. Do not operate the process valve, loosen fittings, drain lines, open filters, prime the pump, remove guards, or reset motor protection. Those actions require a qualified process-maintenance technician and separate approved instructions for isolation, depressurization, and hygiene. A stopped pump does not prove pressure has been removed. Use RES-ST01-001 for the incident-specific assistance route." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/EQ-ST02-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "EQ-ST02-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: EQ-ST02-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Applies to ST02_SEALING. Fictional equipment details and synthetic training instructions; not manufacturer instructions. Existing iMAKS limits are retained. No intrusive repair or isolation sequence is supplied." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/EQ-ST02-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "EQ-ST02-001 §Installed equipment" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST02_SEALING_CUR>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST02_SEALING_TMP>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/TMP-2210>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Installed equipment. ST02_SEALING: Sealing jaw JAW-ST02-01 and heater HTR-ST02-01 are inside a fixed guard. Temperature sensor ST02_SEALING_TMP is the installed ThermoSense TMP-2210, as recorded in this scenario installation register. ST02_SEALING_CUR measures motor current. HMI-ST02 is outside the guard at the operator position. Production order PO-1003 is affected. The replacement Series 2400 mentioned in DS-THERM-2200 is a recommendation, not the installed sensor." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/EQ-ST02-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "EQ-ST02-001 §Controls and observation point" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Controls and observation point. ST02_SEALING: HMI-ST02 provides Diagnostics, Alarm History, Stop, and Alarm Acknowledge. OBS-ST02-01 is the marked position outside the closed guard facing the jaw inspection window. Read temperatures from HMI-ST02; do not touch the jaw or sensor, and do not open guards. An emergency-stop control is next to the panel. Acknowledge records receipt; it does not reset a trip or authorize restart." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/EQ-ST02-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "EQ-ST02-001 §Lone-worker scope" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Lone-worker scope. ST02_SEALING: The trained line operator may read diagnostics, stop the station with the documented Stop control, record evidence, and observe from OBS-ST02-01. Sensor replacement, parameter edits, electrical measurements, heater adjustment, and guarded access require a qualified technician and the separate approved isolation instruction. A stopped machine can remain hot and energized. Contact fictional Maintenance Desk extension 240; if unavailable, retain the stop and log the attempt." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/EQ-ST04-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "EQ-ST04-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: EQ-ST04-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Applies to ST04_PACKAGING and production order PO-1005. This is fictional equipment and synthetic training documentation. Component locations and controls below are invented for this demo; they are not manufacturer instructions. The scenario supplements SOP-001, SOP-002, and SOP-003 without changing their alarm limits." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/EQ-ST04-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "EQ-ST04-001 §Component locations" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_CUR>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_SPD>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_VIB>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/VIB-4480>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Component locations. ST04_PACKAGING transfers sealed trays to the final packaging outlet. The operator position faces the outlet. The operator panel HMI-ST04 is outside the fixed guard on the outlet side. Main bearing BRG-ST04-01 is at the drive end, behind the fixed guard. Sensor ST04_PACKAGING_VIB, model VIB-4480, is mounted on that bearing housing. ST04_PACKAGING_SPD measures conveyor speed; ST04_PACKAGING_CUR measures motor current. These identifiers refer to the same sensors in the telemetry records." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/EQ-ST04-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "EQ-ST04-001 §Operator controls and inspection points" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Operator controls and inspection points. ST04_PACKAGING HMI-ST04 has read-only Diagnostics, Alarm History, and Maintenance History pages, plus Stop and Alarm Acknowledge controls. The outside observation point OBS-ST04-01 faces the drive-end inspection window without entering a guarded area. A local emergency-stop button is beside HMI-ST04. Alarm acknowledgement records that the operator has seen an alarm; it does not clear the underlying fault, release an emergency stop, or authorize restart." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/EQ-ST04-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "EQ-ST04-001 §Lone-worker scope" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Lone-worker scope. For ST04_PACKAGING, the scenario assumes a trained line operator is alone and may read diagnostics, record observations, and observe from OBS-ST04-01 with guards closed. The operator may not open guards, reach into the conveyor, remove trapped material, lubricate the bearing, open electrical panels, or perform a test run after a critical vibration trip alone. A stopped conveyor is not evidence of energy isolation. Intrusive work requires a qualified technician following the site's approved isolation procedure; that procedure is outside this dataset." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/EQ-ST04-001-s5> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "EQ-ST04-001 §Required resources" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Required resources. For external checks of ST04_PACKAGING, use HMI-ST04 and the incident log; no hand tools are required. Do not approach the drive to take manual readings. Record the sensor ID, timestamp, value, unit, quality flag, machine state, and whether each value was measured while running or stopped. Remote maintenance advice is available through the fictional internal Maintenance Desk extension 240; if unavailable, retain the stop and log the attempted contact. No response time or remote restart authority is promised." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/EVT-ST01-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "EVT-ST01-001 §EVT-ST01-001-A" ;
