    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/HIST-ST01-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "HIST-ST01-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: HIST-ST01-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Applies to ST01_FILLING. Fictional equipment details and synthetic training instructions; not manufacturer instructions. Existing iMAKS limits are retained. No intrusive repair or isolation sequence is supplied." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/HIST-ST01-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "HIST-ST01-001 §WO-ST01-301: restricted inlet filter" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "WO-ST01-301: restricted inlet filter. ST01_FILLING: On 2026-09-20 low pressure and flow occurred at ST01_FILLING. A qualified technician measured filter differential pressure under a separate approved instruction and confirmed restriction in FLT-ST01-01. The filter was replaced and hygiene/verification records completed before release. No differential-pressure measurement is supplied for INC-ST01-20261024-01, so the same repair cannot be selected automatically." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/HIST-ST01-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "HIST-ST01-001 §WO-ST01-319: pump delivery issue" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "WO-ST01-319: pump delivery issue. ST01_FILLING: On 2026-10-11 low pressure and flow with the valve indicated open was traced to a pump fault after qualified inspection. A pump repair and supervised verification restored nominal delivery. The older confirmed cause does not establish PMP-ST01-01 condition in the current incident." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/HIST-ST01-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "HIST-ST01-001 §Open incident boundary" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/maintenance/MAINT-04>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/MAINT-04>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Open incident boundary. ST01_FILLING: As of 2026-10-24T13:00:05+02:00, INC-ST01-20261024-01 has no observed inlet position, pump-status reading, filter differential pressure, upstream-pressure measurement, confirmed cause, repair completion, or release approval. The provided sparse telemetry cannot establish a continuous fifteen-minute MAINT-04 trigger." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/HIST-ST02-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "HIST-ST02-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: HIST-ST02-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Applies to ST02_SEALING. Fictional equipment details and synthetic training instructions; not manufacturer instructions. Existing iMAKS limits are retained. No intrusive repair or isolation sequence is supplied." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/HIST-ST02-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "HIST-ST02-001 §WO-ST02-201: prior setting error" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "WO-ST02-201: prior setting error. ST02_SEALING: On 2026-09-15 a qualified technician confirmed an incorrect recipe setting after a changeover. The setting was restored under a separately approved instruction and a supervised verification was recorded. The order was closed that day. No setting error is confirmed for INC-ST02-20261024-01; its current setpoint is not supplied." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/HIST-ST02-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "HIST-ST02-001 §WO-ST02-217: prior sensor drift" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/TMP-2210>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "WO-ST02-217: prior sensor drift. ST02_SEALING: On 2026-10-06 an independent calibrated reference confirmed drift in a previous TMP-2210 sensor. A qualified technician replaced it with the same model and documented verification at 185 degrees C. This report does not authorize operation above 200 degrees C and does not prove the currently installed sensor is drifting." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/HIST-ST02-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "HIST-ST02-001 §Current incident boundary" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Current incident boundary. ST02_SEALING: As of 2026-10-24T12:00:05+02:00, INC-ST02-20261024-01 has no independent temperature measurement, confirmed cause, completed corrective work, engineering change, test authorization, or production release. Historical closure records cannot close the present incident." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/HIST-ST04-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "HIST-ST04-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_VIB>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: HIST-ST04-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Fictional completed work reports for ST04_PACKAGING, BRG-ST04-01, and ST04_PACKAGING_VIB. Historical readings are not live measurements. These reports establish previous findings only." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/HIST-ST04-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "HIST-ST04-001 §WO-ST04-101: lubrication deficiency" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/maintenance/MAINT-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/MAINT-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_SPD>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_VIB> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "WO-ST04-101: lubrication deficiency. On 2026-09-18, ST04_PACKAGING_VIB increased from 0.13 to 0.24 mm/s while ST04_PACKAGING_SPD remained 1.20 m/s. After approved isolation, a qualified technician confirmed insufficient lubrication at BRG-ST04-01 and performed MAINT-01 using the separate approved maintenance instruction. A supervised post-work test measured 0.12 mm/s at 1.20 m/s. The report was closed on 2026-09-18. This finding does not establish the cause of INC-ST04-20261024-01." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/HIST-ST04-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "HIST-ST04-001 §WO-ST04-118: sensor mounting fault" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_VIB> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "WO-ST04-118: sensor mounting fault. On 2026-10-09, ST04_PACKAGING_VIB showed intermittent high readings while speed and current remained stable. Under approved isolation, a qualified technician found a loose sensor mounting at BRG-ST04-01, restored it under the manufacturer's instruction, and verified the signal. The report was closed after a supervised test at 0.12 mm/s and 1.20 m/s. No bearing defect was confirmed. Similar telemetry alone cannot distinguish this issue from a mechanical fault." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/HIST-ST04-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "HIST-ST04-001 §WO-ST04-129: recent visual inspection" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_VIB>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "WO-ST04-129: recent visual inspection. On 2026-10-22, an external visual inspection of ST04_PACKAGING recorded no visible cable damage through the inspection window. No guards were removed, no bearing lubrication was performed, and no internal bearing condition was assessed. ST04_PACKAGING_VIB was 0.12 mm/s at 1.20 m/s at that time. This record cannot exclude a later defect or prove that the bearing is currently serviceable." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/HIST-ST04-001-s5> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "HIST-ST04-001 §Open incident boundary" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Open incident boundary. As of 2026-10-24T10:00:05+02:00, INC-ST04-20261024-01 at ST04_PACKAGING has no confirmed root cause, completed repair, technician inspection, or restart approval in this dataset. Do not reuse the closed status or successful test readings of an older work order as evidence that the current incident is resolved." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/REC-ST01-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "REC-ST01-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: REC-ST01-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Applies to ST01_FILLING. Fictional equipment details and synthetic training instructions; not manufacturer instructions. Existing iMAKS limits are retained. No intrusive repair or isolation sequence is supplied." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/REC-ST01-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "REC-ST01-001 §Station and product hold" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Station and product hold. ST01_FILLING: Keep ST01_FILLING stopped after FILL-PRS-LL. Place output since the first low-pressure observation at 2026-10-24T12:40:00+02:00 under a quality-hold request for PO-1001; Quality must confirm the affected interval because the exact onset between sparse samples is unknown. A hold request is not proof that ERP or physical segregation has already been completed. Do not release product or silently record the request as executed." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/REC-ST01-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "REC-ST01-001 §Prerequisites for a test" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Prerequisites for a test. ST01_FILLING: A qualified process-maintenance technician must record findings, cause assessment, any corrective work, and completion of the separate approved isolation, depressurization, restoration, and hygiene checks. Record any part actually installed. A shift supervisor must authorize the supervised verification; Quality must approve required hygiene clearance. The lone operator cannot substitute remote advice or a stock record for these approvals. Reset, valve operation, repair, and test-start sequences require separate approved machine instructions." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/REC-ST01-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "REC-ST01-001 §Verification criteria" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST01_FILLING_FLW>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST01_FILLING_PRS>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Verification criteria. ST01_FILLING: For this fictional supervised ST01_FILLING test, collect good-quality pressure and flow at intervals no greater than ten seconds for five uninterrupted minutes. ST01_FILLING_PRS must stay within 3.75 to 3.85 bar and ST01_FILLING_FLW within 118.5 to 121.5 L/min, using SOP-002 nominal bands. No active pressure/flow alarms or observed leakage is permitted. A failed criterion or missing sample returns the station to maintenance; do not repeatedly reset. These readings must be measured during the authorized test, not borrowed from historical operation." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/REC-ST01-001-s5> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "REC-ST01-001 §Separate machine and product releases" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Separate machine and product releases. ST01_FILLING: Machine restart requires completed maintenance, hygiene clearance, a passing supervised test, explicit alarm clearance, and shift-supervisor production release. Product release additionally requires Quality approval for the affected interval of PO-1001. No such approvals or post-repair samples exist in INC-ST01-20261024-01. If the specialist cannot attend, the operator checklist ends with checks recorded, assistance requested, and station/product release blocked." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/REC-ST02-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "REC-ST02-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: REC-ST02-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Applies to ST02_SEALING. Fictional equipment details and synthetic training instructions; not manufacturer instructions. Existing iMAKS limits are retained. No intrusive repair or isolation sequence is supplied." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/REC-ST02-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "REC-ST02-001 §Hold and qualified review" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/TMP-2210>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Hold and qualified review. ST02_SEALING: After the reported excursion above the TMP-2210 continuous rating, retain the stop pending qualified maintenance assessment and engineering review of SPEC-ST02-001. The lone operator cannot authorize a test, modify thresholds, or approve a replacement model. Cooling below a limit does not establish instrument accuracy or resolve the protection mismatch." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/REC-ST02-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "REC-ST02-001 §Prerequisites for verification" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Prerequisites for verification. ST02_SEALING: A qualified technician must document the cause assessment, independent temperature verification using the separate approved measurement instruction, any corrective work, and completion of the approved isolation/restoration process. Engineering must record an approved disposition of the protection mismatch, including applicable instrument, operating limits, and controller protection. The shift supervisor must authorize a controlled verification test; all guards and protective functions must be restored. The physical repair, test-start, and reset sequences are outside this dataset." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/REC-ST02-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "REC-ST02-001 §Verification and release" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Verification and release. ST02_SEALING: For the fictional supervised verification at a target of 185 degrees C, record good-quality control readings and an independent reference at intervals no greater than ten seconds for five uninterrupted minutes. Both must stay within 183.8 to 186.2 degrees C, and their difference must not exceed the DS-THERM-2200 accuracy of 1.5 degrees C. An invalid sample, missing reference, alarm, or failed criterion returns the station to maintenance. These acceptance criteria do not resolve the protection mismatch by themselves. Explicit alarm clearance, qualified maintenance confirmation, engineering disposition, and supervisor production release are required. None is supplied for this incident." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/REC-ST04-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "REC-ST04-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/maintenance/MAINT-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/MAINT-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/RULE-ST04-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/RULE-ST04-02>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: REC-ST04-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Fictional release rules for ST04_PACKAGING following a vibration alarm. Supplements RULE-ST04-01, RULE-ST04-02, and MAINT-01. This document states acceptance criteria; it is not an isolation, repair, or controller-reset instruction." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/REC-ST04-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "REC-ST04-001 §Hold after critical vibration" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Hold after critical vibration. After PKG-VIB-HH at ST04_PACKAGING, keep the station stopped until a qualified technician has assessed the cause and the shift supervisor has authorized a controlled verification test. An operator working alone cannot grant these approvals. Alarm acknowledgement, zero vibration at zero speed, an old successful work order, and an absence of visible damage do not satisfy release conditions. If assistance is unavailable, the checklist ends with the machine stopped and maintenance pending." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/REC-ST04-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "REC-ST04-001 §Prerequisites for a controlled verification test" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Prerequisites for a controlled verification test. For ST04_PACKAGING, the maintenance record must identify the incident, inspection findings, any corrective work, and the qualified technician responsible. The technician must confirm completion of the approved isolation and restoration process, guards restored, personnel clear, and protective functions available. The shift supervisor must record test authorization. No test may start with missing prerequisites. The actual restoration, reset, and start sequence must come from the separate approved machine instruction; it is not supplied here." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/REC-ST04-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "REC-ST04-001 §Verification acceptance criteria" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_CUR>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_SPD>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_VIB>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Verification acceptance criteria. For an authorized supervised ST04_PACKAGING test at the documented reference speed of 1.20 m/s, collect good-quality ST04_PACKAGING_VIB, ST04_PACKAGING_SPD, and ST04_PACKAGING_CUR samples at intervals no greater than 10 seconds for five uninterrupted minutes. Vibration must remain within 0.115 to 0.125 mm/s, speed within 1.18 to 1.22 m/s, and current within 8.5 to 8.9 A. These fictional test criteria use the existing SOP-002 nominal bands and are stricter than warning limits. No active vibration alarm, unexpected noise, or visible abnormal movement is permitted. If any criterion fails or a sample gap exceeds 10 seconds, stop the test and return the incident to maintenance; do not repeatedly reset." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/REC-ST04-001-s5> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "REC-ST04-001 §Production release and incident closure" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Production release and incident closure. For ST04_PACKAGING, the shift supervisor records production release only after the authorized verification test passes and the alarm lifecycle explicitly records clearance. Record test start/end, measurement references, work-order reference, technician confirmation, supervisor approval, and release time. Until those records exist, report restart blocked. INC-ST04-20261024-01 supplies no post-repair test, repair completion, alarm clearance, or release record; checklist generation must not claim successful recovery." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/RES-ST01-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "RES-ST01-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: RES-ST01-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Applies to ST01_FILLING. Fictional equipment details and synthetic training instructions; not manufacturer instructions. Existing iMAKS limits are retained. No intrusive repair or isolation sequence is supplied." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/RES-ST01-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "RES-ST01-001 §Snapshot validity" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Snapshot validity. ST01_FILLING: Synthetic assistance and inventory snapshot observed at 2026-10-24T13:00:05+02:00 and valid until 2026-10-24T13:15:05+02:00 for INC-ST01-20261024-01. Reconfirm after expiry. These are scenario-only personnel identifiers, not identities from the iMAKS registry. Only the trained line operator is physically present; no on-site process-maintenance technician or release approver is confirmed." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/RES-ST01-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "RES-ST01-001 §Usual specialist unavailable" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Usual specialist unavailable. ST01_FILLING: EMP-DEMO-201, Maya Reed, is the usual qualified process-maintenance specialist for ST01_FILLING. Her recorded shift ended at 12:00 on 2026-10-24. At the snapshot time she is off shift and unavailable; do not recommend her as an available on-site helper. The line operator has no documented qualification to open filters, service pumps, or enter guarded areas." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/RES-ST01-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "RES-ST01-001 §Remote fallback" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Remote fallback. ST01_FILLING: Fictional Kelvara Maintenance Desk extension 240 routes to service ticket queue SVC-ST01. On-call process service is scheduled for remote triage from 12:00 to 16:00 on 2026-10-24. A scheduled service route is not a confirmed answered call or a dispatched technician. Site attendance, arrival time, and diagnosis are unknown. Request a callback, record the attempt and response, and retain the stop if assistance is unavailable. A remote advisor does not grant the operator intrusive-work qualifications." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/RES-ST01-001-s5> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "RES-ST01-001 §Spare stock and applicability" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Spare stock and applicability. ST01_FILLING: Inventory snapshot: one sealed filter cartridge PART-FLT-ST01-A, listed for housing FLT-ST01-01, at stores bin B-14; zero pump assembly PART-PMP-ST01-A. No part is reserved or issued. A qualified technician must verify installed housing compatibility and approved hygiene requirements before selection. The availability of a filter cartridge does not establish filter restriction, authorize its installation by the lone operator, or prove the station is repairable with current stock." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/SOP-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "SOP-001 §1. Station Dependencies" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/CAF01_CAFETERIA>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/CHM01_CHEMICALSTORAGE>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/RND01_RDLAB>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/SRV01_SERVERROOM>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST03_LABELLING>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/WRH01_WAREHOUSE>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/zone/Cafeteria>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/zone/Chemical_Storage>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/zone/General_Warehouse>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/zone/Production_Area>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/zone/R_D_Lab>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/zone/Server_Room> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "1. Station Dependencies ST01_FILLING → ST02_SEALING → ST03_LABELLING → ST04_PACKAGING. A fault at any station propagates downstream unless the line is halted. Station ID Zone Depends On Downstream Effect ST01_FILLING Production Area — Feeds ST02_SEALING ST02_SEALING Production Area ST01 Feeds ST03; thermal fault → ST04 speed reduction ST03_LABELLING Production Area ST02 Feeds ST04_PACKAGING ST04_PACKAGING Production Area ST03 Final output SRV01_SERVERROOM Server Room HVAC SCADA control; failure → line halt WRH01_WAREHOUSE General Warehouse COMPRESSOR Cold storage — product quality CHM01_CHEMICALSTORAGE Chemical Storage HVAC Hazardous materials — safety critical RND01_RDLAB R&D Lab HVAC Precision experiments — climate sensitive CAF01_CAFETERIA Cafeteria HVAC Occupant comfort — food safety" .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/SOP-004-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "SOP-004 §1. Role-Zone Authorisation Matrix" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/zone/Cafeteria>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/zone/R_D_Lab>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/zone/Server_Room> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "1. Role-Zone Authorisation Matrix Role Prod. Area Server Room Gen. Warehous e Main Entranc e Chem. Stora ge R&D Lab Cafeteria operator YES NO YES YES NO NO YES technician YES YES YES YES YES YES YES supervisor YES YES YES YES YES YES YES manager YES YES YES YES YES YES YES security YES YES YES YES YES YES YES visitor YES NO NO YES NO NO YES" .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/SPEC-ST02-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "SPEC-ST02-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: SPEC-ST02-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Applies to ST02_SEALING. Fictional equipment details and synthetic training instructions; not manufacturer instructions. Existing iMAKS limits are retained. No intrusive repair or isolation sequence is supplied." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/SPEC-ST02-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "SPEC-ST02-001 §Applicable sources" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/RULE-ST02-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/RULE-ST02-02>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST02_SEALING_TMP>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/TMP-2210>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Applicable sources. ST02_SEALING: The installed ST02_SEALING_TMP model is TMP-2210 per EQ-ST02-001. DS-THERM-2200 specifies 200 degrees C continuous maximum and 220 degrees C intermittent for less than ten minutes, not for control. SOP-001 RULE-ST02-01 gives an operating band of 175 to 195 degrees C; RULE-ST02-02 and SOP-002 give a critical threshold above 210 degrees C. The three numbers have different meanings and must be cited separately." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/SPEC-ST02-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "SPEC-ST02-001 §Protection gap and decision" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/TMP-2210>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Protection gap and decision. ST02_SEALING: A 210 degrees C critical threshold does not make continuous operation up to 210 degrees C acceptable for TMP-2210. At the replay peak of 205 degrees C, the approved operating band and the continuous instrument rating are already exceeded although the critical threshold has not been crossed. Surface this protection mismatch rather than treating absence of a critical alarm as permission to continue. The intermittent 220 degrees C note cannot authorize process control at 205 degrees C." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/SPEC-ST02-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "SPEC-ST02-001 §Revision and applicability" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Revision and applicability. ST02_SEALING: This synthetic applicability note is revision 1, effective 2026-10-24. It records the mismatch; it does not change SOP-001, SOP-002, or DS-THERM-2200, approve a new threshold, or certify a sensor replacement. No approved engineering change, installed replacement, independent reference measurement, or revised control configuration is included for INC-ST02-20261024-01. Any proposed higher-rated model in the graph must not be treated as installed equipment." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TEL-ST01-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TEL-ST01-001 §Machine observations" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST01_FILLING_FLW>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST01_FILLING_PRS>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Synthetic replay for ST01_FILLING, incident INC-ST01-20261024-01, order PO-1001. Selected time: 2026-10-24T13:00:05+02:00. This source provides observations, not repair or restart approval. Latest snapshot fresh with good quality: True. TEL-ST01-001 at 2026-10-24T12:30:00+02:00: state=RUNNING; ST01_FILLING_PRS=3.8 bar (quality=good); ST01_FILLING_FLW=120.0 L/min (quality=good). TEL-ST01-002 at 2026-10-24T12:40:00+02:00: state=RUNNING; ST01_FILLING_PRS=3.2 bar (quality=good); ST01_FILLING_FLW=115.0 L/min (quality=good). TEL-ST01-003 at 2026-10-24T13:00:00+02:00: state=RUNNING; ST01_FILLING_PRS=2.9 bar (quality=good); ST01_FILLING_FLW=110.0 L/min (quality=good). TEL-ST01-004 at 2026-10-24T13:00:05+02:00: state=STOPPED_QUALITY_HOLD; ST01_FILLING_PRS=2.8 bar (quality=good); ST01_FILLING_FLW=0.0 L/min (quality=good). Stopped readings do not establish recovery. Sparse historical observations; no continuous-duration proof or post-repair verification test. A good controller quality flag does not certify instrument accuracy outside its specified range." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TEL-ST02-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TEL-ST02-001 §Machine observations" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST02_SEALING_CUR>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST02_SEALING_TMP>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Synthetic replay for ST02_SEALING, incident INC-ST02-20261024-01, order PO-1003. Selected time: 2026-10-24T12:00:05+02:00. This source provides observations, not repair or restart approval. Latest snapshot fresh with good quality: True. TEL-ST02-001 at 2026-10-24T11:50:00+02:00: state=RUNNING; ST02_SEALING_TMP=185.0 degC (quality=good); ST02_SEALING_CUR=12.4 A (quality=good). TEL-ST02-002 at 2026-10-24T11:55:00+02:00: state=RUNNING; ST02_SEALING_TMP=198.0 degC (quality=good); ST02_SEALING_CUR=12.4 A (quality=good). TEL-ST02-003 at 2026-10-24T12:00:00+02:00: state=RUNNING; ST02_SEALING_TMP=205.0 degC (quality=good); ST02_SEALING_CUR=12.4 A (quality=good). TEL-ST02-004 at 2026-10-24T12:00:05+02:00: state=STOPPED_OPERATOR; ST02_SEALING_TMP=204.0 degC (quality=good); ST02_SEALING_CUR=0.0 A (quality=good). Stopped readings do not establish recovery. Sparse historical observations; no continuous-duration proof or post-repair verification test. A good controller quality flag does not certify instrument accuracy outside its specified range." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TEL-ST04-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TEL-ST04-001 §Machine observations" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_CUR>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_SPD>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_VIB>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Synthetic replay for ST04_PACKAGING, incident INC-ST04-20261024-01, order PO-1005. Selected time: 2026-10-24T10:00:05+02:00. This source provides observations, not repair or restart approval. Latest snapshot fresh with good quality: True. TEL-ST04-001 at 2026-10-24T09:00:00+02:00: state=RUNNING; ST04_PACKAGING_VIB=0.12 mm/s (quality=good); ST04_PACKAGING_SPD=1.2 m/s (quality=good); ST04_PACKAGING_CUR=8.7 A (quality=good). TEL-ST04-002 at 2026-10-24T09:30:00+02:00: state=RUNNING; ST04_PACKAGING_VIB=0.16 mm/s (quality=good); ST04_PACKAGING_SPD=1.2 m/s (quality=good); ST04_PACKAGING_CUR=8.7 A (quality=good). TEL-ST04-003 at 2026-10-24T09:50:00+02:00: state=RUNNING; ST04_PACKAGING_VIB=0.23 mm/s (quality=good); ST04_PACKAGING_SPD=1.2 m/s (quality=good); ST04_PACKAGING_CUR=8.8 A (quality=good). TEL-ST04-004 at 2026-10-24T09:59:50+02:00: state=RUNNING; ST04_PACKAGING_VIB=0.32 mm/s (quality=good); ST04_PACKAGING_SPD=1.2 m/s (quality=good); ST04_PACKAGING_CUR=8.8 A (quality=good). TEL-ST04-005 at 2026-10-24T10:00:00+02:00: state=RUNNING; ST04_PACKAGING_VIB=0.38 mm/s (quality=good); ST04_PACKAGING_SPD=1.2 m/s (quality=good); ST04_PACKAGING_CUR=8.9 A (quality=good). TEL-ST04-006 at 2026-10-24T10:00:05+02:00: state=STOPPED_PROTECTIVE; ST04_PACKAGING_VIB=0.0 mm/s (quality=good); ST04_PACKAGING_SPD=0.0 m/s (quality=good); ST04_PACKAGING_CUR=0.0 A (quality=good). Stopped readings do not establish recovery. Sparse historical samples plus the incident snapshot; not a continuous stream and not a post-repair verification test." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST01-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST01-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: TRB-ST01-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Applies to ST01_FILLING. Fictional equipment details and synthetic training instructions; not manufacturer instructions. Existing iMAKS limits are retained. No intrusive repair or isolation sequence is supplied." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST01-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST01-001 §Step 1: confirm the stop" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST01_FILLING_FLW>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST01_FILLING_PRS>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 1: confirm the stop. ST01_FILLING: At HMI-ST01 Diagnostics, record state, timestamp, quality, ST01_FILLING_PRS, and ST01_FILLING_FLW. After FILL-PRS-LL, expected replay state is STOPPED_QUALITY_HOLD and flow is 0.0 L/min. If state is missing or inconsistent, retain the hold and request assistance; do not approach process equipment to compensate for missing data. For an immediate hazard use the emergency stop and keep clear." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST01-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST01-001 §Step 2: preserve the incident evidence" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 2: preserve the incident evidence. ST01_FILLING: In Alarm History, record instance IDs, codes, times, trigger samples, and whether alarms are still active. Record the last running pressure and flow separately from stopped readings. Compare them with ALM-ST01-001. Acknowledge only after recording; do not reset or resume filling. The replay first shows low pressure at 12:40 and the critical event at 13:00; it does not record that the five-minute inlet check was performed." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST01-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST01-001 §Step 3: inspect the external inlet indicator" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 3: inspect the external inlet indicator. ST01_FILLING: From OBS-ST01-01 with the station stopped and guards closed, read the VLV-ST01-01 position indicator. If CLOSED, report a possible supply-path issue without opening the valve. If OPEN, record it and continue to the pump-status observation; an open indicator does not prove supply or filter condition. If UNKNOWN or not visible, record the missing observation and escalate. No actual valve-position observation is included in this incident dataset." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST01-001-s5> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST01-001 §Step 4: read pump status and look for external evidence" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 4: read pump status and look for external evidence. ST01_FILLING: At OBS-ST01-01 read the PMP-ST01-01 status lamp as normal, fault, or not visible. If fault, record the displayed code if readable from the HMI; do not reset motor protection. If normal, compare prior running pressure and flow while keeping the stop; normal status does not prove pump delivery. From outside the guard record visible leakage or abnormal accumulation as observed, not observed, or not visible. Do not touch fluid or open fittings. Pump status and leakage observations are not supplied for this incident." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST01-001-s6> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST01-001 §Step 5: assess the diagnostic branches" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/maintenance/MAINT-04>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/MAINT-04>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 5: assess the diagnostic branches. ST01_FILLING: If inlet indication is closed or unknown, qualified inspection of supply path and valve is required. If indication is open and pump status is fault, qualified pump/drive assessment is required. If indication is open with normal pump status but running pressure and flow were low, filter restriction, upstream supply loss, and pump delivery remain competing hypotheses. Without upstream or filter differential-pressure readings, do not select one as confirmed. Read HIST-ST01-001 for prior findings and its limits. Do not report that MAINT-04 duration is proven from sparse samples." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST01-001-s7> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST01-001 §Step 6: use the available support route" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST01_FILLING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 6: use the available support route. ST01_FILLING: Consult RES-ST01-001 at the same selected time. The usual specialist is off shift; the on-call service can receive a remote triage call, but attendance and arrival are unconfirmed. Contact the stated service route with pressure/flow evidence and missing observations. Keep the product and station on hold under REC-ST01-001. Stock availability alone is not permission to replace a part. If no response is obtained, record the attempted call and leave the hold in place." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST02-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST02-001 §Scope and document control" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and document control. Document ID: TRB-ST02-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Applies to ST02_SEALING. Fictional equipment details and synthetic training instructions; not manufacturer instructions. Existing iMAKS limits are retained. No intrusive repair or isolation sequence is supplied." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST02-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST02-001 §Step 1: establish state and timestamp" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST02_SEALING_TMP>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 1: establish state and timestamp. ST02_SEALING: At HMI-ST02 Diagnostics, record the selected time, machine state, ST02_SEALING_TMP reading, timestamp, and quality. Use ALM-ST02-001 freshness rules. If missing or stale, do not claim the station is safe; contact Maintenance Desk 240. In an actual running over-temperature condition, use the normal Stop control from outside the guard. If an immediate hazard is present, use the emergency stop and keep clear." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST02-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST02-001 §Step 2: record the temperature history" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 2: record the temperature history. ST02_SEALING: Open Alarm History and the temperature trend. Record each alarm instance, activation time, trigger sample, peak temperature, operating setpoint if visible, and controller action. Do not change the setpoint or acknowledge away the evidence. An absent setpoint in the replay is unknown. Distinguish the running peak from the later cooling observation and document whether state STOPPED_OPERATOR is supported by fresh telemetry." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST02-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST02-001 §Step 3: compare all three limits" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/TMP-2210>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 3: compare all three limits. ST02_SEALING: Using SPEC-ST02-001, compare the observed running peak with the 195 degrees C operating-band ceiling, the 200 degrees C TMP-2210 continuous rating, and the 210 degrees C critical threshold. At 205 degrees C report both exceeded limits and the not-yet-triggered critical threshold. Flag the protection mismatch. Do not describe the reading as a verified true temperature or use the intermittent rating to justify operation." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST02-001-s5> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST02-001 §Step 4: inspect externally" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 4: inspect externally. ST02_SEALING: From OBS-ST02-01 outside closed guards, note visible product accumulation, unusual discoloration, or visible cable damage as observed, not observed, or not visible. Do not touch surfaces, remove trays, open guards, or inspect energized circuits. If smoke or another immediate hazard appears, withdraw and follow site emergency arrangements. Lack of visible damage does not establish heater or sensor integrity." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST02-001-s6> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST02-001 §Step 5: separate hypotheses and escalation" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 5: separate hypotheses and escalation. ST02_SEALING: Read HIST-ST02-001. A previous controller setting error or sensor drift is only a hypothesis for this incident. Retain the stop and contact Maintenance Desk 240 with the instrument model, peak, three limits, active alarm IDs, and observed state. Request qualified verification of instrument validity and engineering review of protection applicability. No automatic parameter change or sensor substitution is authorized." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST02-001-s7> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST02-001 §Step 6: record restart blockers" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST02_SEALING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 6: record restart blockers. ST02_SEALING: Apply REC-ST02-001. Record absent independent measurement, unconfirmed cause, missing corrective-work record, unresolved protection mismatch, and missing release approvals. The operator alone cannot clear these blockers. Leave the station stopped and log the handover attempt if assistance is unavailable. Do not claim cooling resolves the mismatch." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST04-001-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST04-001 §Scope and entry condition" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Scope and entry condition. Document ID: TRB-ST04-001. Revision: 1. Effective date: 2026-10-24. Owner: Kelvara Maintenance Engineering. Synthetic procedure for a trained lone operator responding to ST04_PACKAGING vibration alarms. Use EQ-ST04-001 for locations, ALM-ST04-001 for thresholds, and REC-ST04-001 for restart restrictions. Perform only external observations; detailed intrusive maintenance is not covered." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST04-001-s2> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST04-001 §Step 1: confirm machine state" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_SPD>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 1: confirm machine state. At HMI-ST04, open Diagnostics for ST04_PACKAGING. Record the machine state, ST04_PACKAGING_SPD, measurement timestamp, and quality. Expected after a critical trip: state STOPPED_PROTECTIVE and speed 0.00 m/s, supported by fresh good-quality data. Confirm visually from outside the guard. If movement continues or an immediate hazard is present, use the local emergency stop and keep clear. If state or speed cannot be established, keep clear and contact Maintenance Desk 240. Do not proceed toward equipment to resolve missing telemetry." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST04-001-s3> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST04-001 §Step 2: preserve alarm evidence" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 2: preserve alarm evidence. At HMI-ST04 Alarm History, record the ST04_PACKAGING alarm instance ID, code, activation time, trigger measurement ID, and active/cleared status. Compare the trigger value against ALM-ST04-001. Acknowledge the displayed alarm only after recording it; acknowledgement is not a reset. For PKG-VIB-HH, retain the stop even if stopped vibration is now zero. If the live display disagrees with the recorded event, retain both records and report the discrepancy rather than selecting one silently." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST04-001-s4> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST04-001 §Step 3: check trend and data quality" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/maintenance/MAINT-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/MAINT-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_CUR>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_SPD>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensor/ST04_PACKAGING_VIB> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 3: check trend and data quality. Read the ST04_PACKAGING_VIB trend alongside ST04_PACKAGING_SPD and ST04_PACKAGING_CUR. Compare good-quality running readings at the same speed across the prior 60 minutes. Record the starting and ending vibration values and their difference. A rise greater than 0.05 mm/s supports MAINT-01. Do not include the stopped sample in that comparison. If timestamps, units, quality, or comparable operating conditions are missing, report that the trend cannot be established. Do not infer a confirmed bearing failure from the trend." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST04-001-s5> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST04-001 §Step 4: observe without entering" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 4: observe without entering. With ST04_PACKAGING stopped, remain at OBS-ST04-01 outside closed guards. Look through the inspection window for displaced trays, visible debris, or visible sensor-cable damage. Record each finding as observed, not observed, or not visible. Do not touch the bearing housing, reach through openings, remove material, or open guards. If smoke, burning smell, or another immediate hazard is present, withdraw and follow site emergency arrangements. If the view is blocked, record not visible; do not treat that as no obstruction." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST04-001-s6> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST04-001 §Step 5: review history and select the next action" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/maintenance/MAINT-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/MAINT-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/rule/RULE-ST04-01>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 5: review history and select the next action. Open ST04_PACKAGING Maintenance History and compare symptoms with HIST-ST04-001. Previous lubrication or sensor-mount faults are possibilities, not the diagnosis of this incident. For a critical alarm, or a visible defect, retain the stop and request qualified maintenance. For warning-only evidence, follow RULE-ST04-01's maintenance scheduling requirement; this procedure grants no independent restart permission. Do not apply the previous repair automatically. MAINT-01 inspection and lubrication require the qualified technician and approved isolation procedure described in EQ-ST04-001." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/TRB-ST04-001-s7> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "TRB-ST04-001 §Step 6: hand over and record the blocker" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/station/ST04_PACKAGING> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "Step 6: hand over and record the blocker. For ST04_PACKAGING, contact Maintenance Desk 240 with the incident ID, alarm instance, pre-stop peak, speed/current at that time, trend comparison, machine state, and external observations. State explicitly that the operator is alone. If no technician is available, leave the machine stopped and record maintenance pending. Follow REC-ST04-001 for release conditions. End the operator checklist with the current blocker; do not invent completed repairs, measurements, or approval." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/document/ALM-ST01-001> a ns1:Document ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST01-001 ST01 Pressure and Flow Alarm Reference" ;
        rdfs:comment "ST01 Pressure and Flow Alarm Reference" ;
        ns1:file "ST01_AlarmReference.md" ;
        ns1:has_chunk <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST01-001-s1>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST01-001-s2>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST01-001-s3>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST01-001-s4>,
            <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/ALM-ST01-001-s5> .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/document/ALM-ST02-001> a ns1:Document ;
        rdfs:label "ALM-ST02-001 ST02 Temperature Alarm Reference" ;
